NAME
       pvresize - tell LVM that a physical volume changed size

SYNOPSIS
       pvresize [--setphysicalvolumesize SIZE] PV...

DESCRIPTION
       After the device under a PV grew (a bigger virtual disk, a partition
       made larger with parted resizepart), pvresize lets LVM use the new
       space: the PV, and so its volume group, gets more free extents.

OPTIONS
       --setphysicalvolumesize SIZE
              Use this size instead of the size of the device (to shrink a PV
              before shrinking its partition). Rarely needed.

EXAMPLES
           pvresize /dev/vdb1
           vgs

SEE ALSO
       pvs(8), vgextend(8), parted(8), lvm(8)
